      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(web): apply Control UI text size to content typography",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where the Appearance text size control persisted a selected value but only visibly affected a narrow part of Control UI typography. Users choosing S, XL, or XXL could still see Settings and most content text rendered at fixed sizes.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThis PR applies the existing `--control-ui-text-scale` token to the Control UI content typography surface: body text, Settings/Appearance forms and cards, quick settings rows, chat message tables/code, and the chat composer. The scope intentionally keeps shell/tool chrome geometry stable rather than scaling every topbar/sidebar control.\n\n## User Impact\n\nChanging Text size in Appearance now produces a visible typography change across the main reading and composing surfaces while preserving the existing layout structure.\n\n## Evidence\n\nValidated locally:\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- Browser smoke with a local CSS harness for S (`0.9`) and XXL (`1.4`): Settings heading changed from `13.5px` to `21px`, chat text from `12.6px` to `19.6px`, quick setting labels from `11.7px` to `18.2px`, and composer text from `16px` to `19.6px`; no horizontal overflow was reported.\n\nNot run:\n\n- Focused Vitest tests, because this worktree has no root `node_modules` and `scripts/run-vitest.mjs` cannot resolve Vitest without installing dependencies.\n- `oxfmt`, because no `oxfmt` binary is available in this worktree.\n",
